'''''Cyperus flavescens''''', commonly known as the '''yellow flatsedge''', is a species of [[flowering plant]] belonging to the family [[Cyperaceae]].

==Taxonomy==
''Cyperus flavescens'' was first [[species description|described]] by the Swedish botanist [[Carl Linnaeus]] in 1753.{{r|IPNI:74698-2}} Linnaeus based his [[:wikt:diagnosis|diagnosis]] on [[Type specimen|specimens]] collected in marshes in Germany, Switzerland, and France ("habitat in Germaniae, Helvetiae, Galliae paludosis").{{sfnp|Linnaeus|1753|loc=[https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/page/358065#page/58/mode/1up pp.&nbsp;46]}}

==Distribution and habitat==
''Cyperus flavescens'' has a [[cosmopolitan distribution]].{{r|POWO:74698-2}} It is native to North America, South America, Europe, Asia, and Africa. It was introduced to [[New South Wales]] and [[Queensland]] in Australia. In North America (north of Mexico), it is most common in the eastern United States.{{r|FNA:242357663|BONAP-state}}

